}+87\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n(y+10{)}^{2}-{10}^{2}+87\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n(y+10{)}^{2}-13.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=10$ and $q=-13.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["4a39d2d9-a85e-5874-9c2e-54401c669388"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "7adfd77a-2c35-5839-aba3-20025a57f8bb" :answer/id #uuid "7adfd77a-2c35-5839-aba3-20025a57f8bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=6,\\,q=23" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "fe944237-c002-5cd8-adbb-4450570fa880" :answer/id #uuid "fe944237-c002-5cd8-adbb-4450570fa880" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=6,\\,q=95" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "8f6f60e3-d6aa-5bae-a63d-aad7f1fb4f10" :answer/id #uuid "8f6f60e3-d6aa-5bae-a63d-aad7f1fb4f10" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=12,\\,q=-85" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "597e36b5-f1c0-5227-ac21-11afe821395b" :answer/id #uuid "597e36b5-f1c0-5227-ac21-11afe821395b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=6,\\,q=53" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "94093a8e-c60a-58df-9727-f636c70bb6d0" :answer/id #uuid "94093a8e-c60a-58df-9727-f636c70bb6d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=6,\\,q=59" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "6496e219-3ebb-5bd6-854b-857232ef2553" :answer-field/id #uuid "6496e219-3ebb-5bd6-854b-857232ef2553" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["7adfd77a-2c35-5839-aba3-20025a57f8bb" "fe944237-c002-5cd8-adbb-4450570fa880" "8f6f60e3-d6aa-5bae-a63d-aad7f1fb4f10" "597e36b5-f1c0-5227-ac21-11afe821395b" "94093a8e-c60a-58df-9727-f636c70bb6d0"] :answer-field/correct "7adfd77a-2c35-5839-aba3-20025a57f8bb" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "ecf84f0e-d57b-5f53-a7ed-0546a4b066ac" :question/id #uuid "ecf84f0e-d57b-5f53-a7ed-0546a4b066ac" :question/problem "If the expression ${y}^{2}+12y+59$ is written as $(y+p{)}^{2}+q,$ then what are the values of $p$ and $q?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}+2\\cdot 6y+59\n$$\n\nNow, here's the trick. We *add* and *then subtract* ${6}^{2},$ writing the constant term $59$ last:\n\n$$\n{{y}^{2}+2\\cdot 6y+{6}^{2}}_{⏟}-\\,{6}^{2}+59\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n(y+6{)}^{2}-{6}^{2}+59\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n(y+6{)}^{2}+23.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=6$ and $q=23.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["6496e219-3ebb-5bd6-854b-857232ef2553"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "9cdabfe5-f04c-5986-ae43-f5e80d28d41e" :answer/id #uuid "9cdabfe5-f04c-5986-ae43-f5e80d28d41e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=6,\\,q=60" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "dd651d16-80af-5212-8e32-b38d7bdac25c" :answer/id #uuid "dd651d16-80af-5212-8e32-b38d7bdac25c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=12,\\,q=-84" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "b0bdb147-02f4-5c04-b7fe-cffda502f599" :answer/id #uuid "b0bdb147-02f4-5c04-b7fe-cffda502f599" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=6,\\,q=96" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "2459506f-d023-5521-91b0-d381e64669a6" :answer/id #uuid "2459506f-d023-5521-91b0-d381e64669a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=6,\\,q=54" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "a3fc207e-1844-5faa-a7af-da246954a3dc" :answer/id #uuid "a3fc207e-1844-5faa-a7af-da246954a3dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=6,\\,q=24" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "0056184b-6afb-5a69-adab-541020c841bb" :answer-field/id #uuid "0056184b-6afb-5a69-adab-541020c841bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["9cdabfe5-f04c-5986-ae43-f5e80d28d41e" "dd651d16-80af-5212-8e32-b38d7bdac25c" "b0bdb147-02f4-